---
import PNotes from "../components/PNotes.astro";
---

<p-slide class="center" autoplay timing="800">
  <h1>🙅‍♂️ <span class="main-gradient">Common Pitfalls</span></h1>
  <h4
    p-fragment
    p-effect="from below"
    class="main-sub-gradient"
    style="padding-inline-end: 0.5em; text-align: end; font-style: italic"
  >
    What Could Go Wrong? <span
      style="-webkit-text-fill-color: initial; font-style: normal">🌚</span
    >
  </h4>
</p-slide>
<p-slide>
  <ul class="space" style="line-height: 1em">
    <li>❌ <span class="main-sub-gradient">Too Many Workers</span></li>
    <li p-fragment p-effect="from right">
      ❌
      <span class="main-sub-gradient">Passing Large Data Objects</span>
    </li>
    <li p-fragment p-effect="from left">
      ❌
      <span class="main-sub-gradient">Memory and performance impact</span>
    </li>
    <li p-fragment p-effect="zoom">
      ❌ <span class="main-sub-gradient"
        >Using Workers for Small, Frequent Tasks</span
      >
    </li>
  </ul>
  <PNotes>
    <ul style="font-size: 0.8em">
      <li>
        Creating a new Web Worker for every small operation can overload the
        system: ✅ Reuse Workers instead of creating a new one each time; ✅ Use
        a Worker Pool
      </li>
      <li>Passing Large Data Objects: use transfer parameter in postMessge</li>
      <li>
        ❌ Communication overhead - Data exchange with the main thread happens
        asynchronously via postMessage(), which can introduce complexity and
        performance overhead.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </PNotes>
</p-slide>
